# MASTER TASK

# Research, Synthesize, Validate, and Build a Production-Grade Architecture Design Skill

You are an autonomous research and knowledge-engineering agent.

Your task is to research real-world architecture, engineering, construction, building science, spatial planning, BIM/CAD, human behavior, operations, and professional architectural practice, then transform the research into a reusable and operational `SKILL.md` for an AI agent that designs buildings.

The target environment is a **grid/tile-based architectural design system**, similar in spatial abstraction to games such as RimWorld or Prison Architect, but the design logic must be grounded in real-world architecture.

---

# 0. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Build an Architecture Design Skill that enables an AI agent to:

```text
Understand requirements
        ↓
Research missing information
        ↓
Analyze site and context
        ↓
Program the building
        ↓
Build spatial relationships
        ↓
Create zoning
        ↓
Design circulation
        ↓
Develop structural and service logic
        ↓
Generate architectural layouts
        ↓
Translate real-world dimensions into grid/tile geometry
        ↓
Validate the design
        ↓
Identify failures
        ↓
Generate alternatives
        ↓
Evaluate trade-offs
        ↓
Iterate
        ↓
Produce a coherent final design
```

The final result must NOT be a generic:

> "Act as a professional architect."

It must be an **operational reasoning framework** that an autonomous agent can execute.

